#
# Showcase: Ramanujan's congruence tau(n) = sigma_11(n) mod 691, as a theorem about the Hecke algebra over Z, computed and
# certified by HACS from the triangulated model of SL_2(Z)\H. Open it in the notebook (Examples...): text cells are typeset,
# and each "Reading the output" panel pairs the mathematics with what HACS computed. The LaTeX switch shows the raw text.
# It runs as a script too (hacs --script showcase_ramanujan_691.oc); every code cell asserts what the text above it states.

# %% [md] Ramanujan's congruence, as a statement about the Hecke algebra over Z
# Let $\Delta = q\prod_{n\ge1}(1-q^n)^{24} = \sum_{n\ge1}\tau(n)\,q^n$ be the discriminant form and
# $E_{12} = 1 + \tfrac{65520}{691}\sum_{n\ge1}\sigma_{11}(n)\,q^n$ the Eisenstein series of weight 12.
# The prime 691 is the numerator of $\zeta(-11) = -\tfrac{B_{12}}{12} = \tfrac{691}{32760}$, and Ramanujan observed
#
# $$\tau(n) \equiv \sigma_{11}(n) \pmod{691}\qquad\text{for all } n \ge 1.$$
#
# Eichler–Shimura puts both forms into one cohomology group: with $V_{10} = \mathrm{Sym}^{10}\mathbb{Z}^2$,
# $H^1(\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}), V_{10}\otimes\mathbb{C}) \cong S_{12}\oplus\overline{S_{12}}\oplus\mathbb{C}E_{12}$, of dimension three.
# Over $\mathbb{Z}$ the congruence becomes a statement about the ring $\mathbb{T}$ generated by the Hecke operators on the
# free part $L = H^1(\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}), V_{10})/\mathrm{tors}$:
#
# > **Statement.**
# > $$\mathbb{T} \;\xrightarrow{\;\sim\;}\; \mathbb{Z}\times_{\mathbb{Z}/691}\mathbb{Z} = \{(a,b)\in\mathbb{Z}^2 : a\equiv b \bmod 691\},\qquad T_n\longmapsto(\sigma_{11}(n),\,\tau(n)),$$
# > and the congruence module is $C_{\mathbb{T}} = \mathbb{T}/(I_{\mathrm{Eis}}+I_{\mathrm{cusp}}) \cong \mathbb{Z}/691$.
#
# The next cells compute and certify this from the triangulated model of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})\backslash\mathfrak{H}$; nothing
# about modular forms goes in. Every formula in a text cell that states a computed fact is checked by an `assert` in the code cell below it.

# %% The cohomology over Z, and the characteristic polynomials of T_p
set coefficient_ring = "Z";
D = descent(1, 10);
display(D.groups_inv[1]);
display(D.charpoly_factored);
assert(D.groups[1] == "Z^3 + Z/2 + Z/2^2 + Z/3", "H^1 = Z^3 + Z/2 + Z/4 + Z/3");
assert(D.charpoly_factored[0].factored == "(X + 24)^2 (X - 2049)", "char_Z(T_2)");
assert(D.charpoly_factored[1].factored == "(X - 252)^2 (X - 177148)", "char_Z(T_3)");
assert(D.charpoly_factored[2].factored == "(X - 4830)^2 (X - 48828126)", "char_Z(T_5)");
for f in D.charpoly_factored { assert(f.verified, "the factors multiply back to char_Z"); }

# %% [md] Reading the output
# | Mathematics | What HACS computed, and how |
# |---|---|
# | $H^1(\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}),V_{10}) \cong \mathbb{Z}^3\oplus\mathbb{Z}/2\oplus\mathbb{Z}/4\oplus\mathbb{Z}/3$. The rank 3 is Eichler–Shimura;
#   the torsion sits at 2 and 3, the primes dividing the orders 4 and 6 of the finite stabilisers. |
#   `descent(1, 10)`: Smith normal forms of the coboundaries over $\mathbb{Z}$, assembled prime by prime from the model.
#   The raw value is `{free_rank: 3, torsion: [[2,1,1],[2,2,1],[3,1,1]]}`; each triple is $(p,k,m)$, meaning $(\mathbb{Z}/p^k)^m$.
#   Contract [C] `sec:integral`; validation `IntegralDescentGroupsValidation`. |
# | The eigenvalues of $T_p$ on $L\otimes\mathbb{C}$ are $\tau(p)$ twice ($\Delta$ and its complex conjugate) and $\sigma_{11}(p)=1+p^{11}$
#   once ($E_{12}$). For example $\tau(2)=-24$ and $1+2^{11}=2049$:
#   $$\operatorname{char}_{\mathbb{Z}}(T_2) = (X+24)^2\,(X-2049).$$ |
#   `charpoly_factored`: $\operatorname{char}_{\mathbb{Z}}(T_p)$ on the free part, factored over $\mathbb{Z}$ (Zassenhaus); the product
#   of the factors is checked against the expanded polynomial (`verified: true`). Validation `IntegralDescentRecordValidation`, arm (Z). |

# %% [md] The congruence, read off the roots
# The two roots of each characteristic polynomial differ by a multiple of 691:
#
# | $p$ | $\tau(p)$ | $\sigma_{11}(p)$ | $(\sigma_{11}(p)-\tau(p))/691$ |
# |---|---|---|---|
# | 2 | $-24$ | 2049 | 3 |
# | 3 | 252 | 177148 | 256 |
# | 5 | 4830 | 48828126 | 70656 |
#
# Three values prove nothing about all $n$. The certified record below works with the whole Hecke algebra.

# %% The table, checked against the roots above
assert(2049 - (-24) == 3 * 691, "p = 2");
assert(177148 - 252 == 256 * 691, "p = 3");
assert(48828126 - 4830 == 70656 * 691, "p = 5");
assert(1 + 2^11 == 2049 and 1 + 3^11 == 177148 and 1 + 5^11 == 48828126, "sigma_11(p) = 1 + p^11");

# %% The Hecke algebra over Z: fibre product and congruence module
R = hecke_structure(1, 10);
display(R.status, R.C_T);
assert(R.status == "final", "the record is final");
assert(R.C_T == "certified:0x2b3" and 0x2b3 == 691, "C_T = Z/691");
fields = ["G3.C_T.exact=0x2b3", "G3.fibre_product=certified", "G3.second_route.ell=691.v_Bk=1", "G3.second_route.ell=691.agrees=true",
          "G2.ell=691.m[0].residue_poly=[24,1]", "G2.ell=691.m[0].local_type.kind=monogenic", "G2.ell=691.m[0].local_type.rank=2",
          "G2.ell=691.m[0].local_type.gorenstein=true", "G2.ell=691.m[0].local_type.hilbert=1,1",
          "G2.ell=691.m[0].components_through.eis=certified", "G2.ell=691.m[0].components_through.cusp=certified",
          "G6.q=1.ell=2.pt[0].split=split_on_P", "G6.q=1.ell=3.pt[0].split=split_on_P"];
for w in fields { k = 0; for s in R.body { if s == w { k = k + 1 } }; assert(k == 1, w); }
display(fields);

# %% [md] Reading the output
# | Mathematics | What HACS computed, and how |
# |---|---|
# | $C_{\mathbb{T}}\cong\mathbb{Z}/691$, and $\mathbb{T}\cong\mathbb{Z}\times_{\mathbb{Z}/691}\mathbb{Z}$, i.e. $\tau(n)\equiv\sigma_{11}(n) \bmod 691$ for **every** $n$. |
#   The record stores `C_T = "certified:0x2b3"` (signed hexadecimal, $\mathtt{0x2b3} = 691$; the page shows the decimal, the stored form on hover).
#   "certified" means that a lower and an upper bound for the order of $C_{\mathbb{T}}$ meet. In the body: `G3.C_T.exact=0x2b3`, `G3.fibre_product=certified`.
#   Contract [C] `def:heckeZcong`, `prop:heckeZcong` (3), (4); validation `HeckeZRecordValidation` (toy cell T1 = (1, 10)). |
# | The second route: $v_{691}(B_{12}/12)=1$, since $B_{12}/12 = -691/32760$. |
#   `G3.second_route.ell=691.v_Bk=1`, `agrees=true`: the congruence module and the Bernoulli number give the same 691-adic valuation. |
# | Locally at 691 there is one maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}=(691,\,T_2+24)$, and
#   $\mathbb{T}_{\mathfrak{m}}\cong\mathbb{Z}_{691}\times_{\mathbb{F}_{691}}\mathbb{Z}_{691}\cong\mathbb{Z}_{691}[x]/(x(x-691))$,
#   which is Gorenstein, with $\mathbb{T}_{\mathfrak{m}}/691 \cong \mathbb{F}_{691}[\varepsilon]/(\varepsilon^2)$. |
#   `G2.ell=691.m[0]`: `residue_poly=[24,1]` (that is $X+24$; coefficients from low to high), `local_type.kind=monogenic`, `rank=2`,
#   `gorenstein=true`, `hilbert=1,1`; `components_through.eis` and `.cusp` both `certified`: both components pass through $\mathfrak{m}$. |
# | Not claimed: that the torsion $\mathbb{Z}/2\oplus\mathbb{Z}/4\oplus\mathbb{Z}/3$ splits off Hecke-equivariantly for all of $\mathbb{T}$. It does for
#   the subalgebra $\mathbb{T}'=\mathbb{Z}[T_2,T_3,T_5]$. |
#   `G6...split=split_on_P` at 2 and 3: "split_on_P" is a statement about $\mathbb{T}'$ only. For all of $\mathbb{T}$ it would need
#   [C] `rmk:heckeZcbthree`, a conjecture. |

# %% [md] Mod 691: the congruence as a non-split extension
# Reduce mod 691. In $H^1 = H^1(\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}),\mathrm{Sym}^{10}\mathbb{F}_{691}^2)$ the interior cohomology $H^1_!$ (the cusp form)
# and the boundary cohomology $H^1_\partial$ (the Eisenstein series) form an exact sequence of Hecke modules
#
# $$0 \longrightarrow H^1_! \longrightarrow H^1 \longrightarrow H^1_\partial \longrightarrow 0, \qquad \dim = 2,\ 3,\ 1 .$$
#
# On both ends $T_p$ acts with the same eigenvalue $1+p^{11}\equiv\tau(p)$. The congruence is visible as the fact that this
# sequence does **not** split: $T_p-(1+p^{11})$ is nilpotent but non-zero on $H^1$, with Jordan type $(2,1)$, and the local
# Hecke algebra mod 691 is $\mathbb{F}_{691}[\varepsilon]/(\varepsilon^2)$.

# %% T_2 mod 691, and the local Hecke algebra
set coefficient_ring = "F_ell";
H = cohomology(symmetric_power(sl2z_model(), 10, 691));
T2 = hecke(H, 2).A(1);
N2 = sub(T2, scale(identity(691, 3), 667));
display(T2, jordan_type(N2));
A = local_algebra(ext_record(10, 691).ideal(0));
display(A);
assert(cone(H).H1_shriek == 2 and boundary(H).dims == [1, 1], "dim H^1_! = 2, dim H^1_bd = 1");
assert(charpoly(T2) == poly(691, [4, 346, 72, 1]) and (2049 + 24) % 691 == 0, "char(T_2) = (X - 667)^3 = (X + 24)^3 over F_691");
assert(N2 != zero(691, 3, 3) and jordan_type(N2) == [2, 1], "T_2 - 667 is nilpotent, non-zero, Jordan type (2, 1)");
assert(A.dim == 2 and A.hilbert == [1, 1] and A.gorenstein, "T_m / 691 = F_691[eps]/eps^2, Gorenstein");

# %% [md] Reading the output
# | Mathematics | What HACS computed, and how |
# |---|---|
# | The entry 23 below the diagonal is the extension class. A complement of $H^1_!$ stable under $T_2$ would make it 0 in a
#   suitable basis, and none exists. |
#   `hecke(H, 2).A(1)`: $T_2$ on $H^1$ in the stored basis. `jordan_type` of the nilpotent part $T_2-667$ ($667\equiv-24\equiv2049$).
#   The same Jordan type holds for $p=3,5,7$ and for $U_{691}-1$ (gallery snippet `ramanujan_10_691`, [PG] `sec:pg-ramanujan`). |
# | $\mathbb{T}_\mathfrak{m}/691 \cong \mathbb{F}_{691}[\varepsilon]/(\varepsilon^2)$, with $\varepsilon$ the image of $T_2+24$. |
#   `ext_record(10, 691)`: one maximal ideal; `local_algebra` reads `dim 2 over F_691, f = 1, embdim 1, nu = 2, Gorenstein`.
#   [E] `cl:ramanujan`; validations `HeckeExtRecordValidation`, `HeckeExtRamanujanValidation`. |

# %% [md] Companion: Mazur's Eisenstein prime at level 11
# The same record at weight 2 and level $\Gamma_0(11)$ (the anemic algebra, generated by the $T_p$ with $p\nmid 11$) gives
#
# $$C_{\mathbb{T}}\cong\mathbb{Z}/5 .$$
#
# This is the congruence $a_p(E)\equiv 1+p \pmod 5$ for the elliptic curve $X_0(11)$; 5 is the numerator of $(11-1)/12$.

# %% C_T at level 11
set coefficient_ring = "Z";
E = hecke_structure(11, 0, "anemic");
display(E.status, E.C_T);
assert(E.status == "final" and E.C_T == "certified:0x5", "Mazur: C_T = Z/5");
